# Secrets. Nothing here should ever exist, but fail closed rather than trust that.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# Raw source data. Reproducible via scripts/fetch_data.ps1, so it does not
# belong in git. The SanctSound FLAC alone is 78 MB, which is past GitHub's
# warning threshold and would bloat every clone for no reason.
data/*.flac
data/*.pdf
data/*.jpg
data/*.png

# Derived clips ARE committed: 1.9 MB each, and they are what the pipeline
# actually reads, so a judge cloning the repo can run the demo without a
# 78 MB download. See the negation below.
!data/reef_window_*.wav

# The NOAA forecast image is committed too, at 534 KB. It is the exact frame
# the vision agent analyzed, it is US Government public domain, and the console
# shows it beside the generated map so a viewer can check the agent's reading
# against the source. A deployed instance that cannot show its own evidence is
# not showing evidence. It is also date-stamped by NOAA and rotates daily, so
# the committed copy IS the artifact.
!data/hab_forecast_cellcounts.png

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
